From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - GProp_VelGProps returns a quantity that
 vanishes at the cylinder limit instead of the volume of a gp_Cone

GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone&, ...) computes

  double ZZ    = (Z2 - Z1) * (Z2 - Z1) * Cnt * Snt;
  double Auxi1 = 2 * R + (Z2 + Z1) * Snt;
  dim          = ZZ * (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Auxi1 / 2.;

which carries a factor of sin a and therefore goes to zero as the semi-angle
does. A cone of vanishing semi-angle is a cylinder, and the gp_Cylinder
overload in the same class answers that exactly with
dim = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) R^2 (Z2 - Z1) / 2, so the two disagree in the limit
where they describe the same solid.

The volume swept between the axis and the cone patch, which is the convention
the cylinder and sphere overloads of this class both use, is the frustum. With
z = v cos a and r(z) = R + v sin a,

  V = int du int r(z)^2 / 2 dz
    = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) cos a / 2 int_{Z1}^{Z2} (R + v sin a)^2 dv
    = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) cos a (Z2 - Z1) (R1^2 + R1 R2 + R2^2) / 6

with R1 = R + Z1 sin a and R2 = R + Z2 sin a, which over a full turn is the
familiar pi H (R1^2 + R1 R2 + R2^2) / 3 with H = (Z2 - Z1) cos a. Expanded in
R and sin a, R1^2 + R1 R2 + R2^2 is

  3 R^2 + 3 R (Z1 + Z2) sin a + (Z1^2 + Z1 Z2 + Z2^2) sin^2 a

which is the form used below, so that the existing R1, R2 and Coef0 locals can
keep their position after dim and the declaration block is left alone. At
a = 0 the expression collapses to (Alpha2 - Alpha1) R^2 (Z2 - Z1) / 2, exactly
the cylinder overload.

GProp_VelGProps and GProp_SelGProps have no caller anywhere in the OCCT tree,
so there is no call site whose use of the result could settle the convention.
The arbiters are therefore the closed form above and the cylinder limit.

Note that the old dim is exactly the old GProp_SelGProps cone dim times
(Z2 - Z1) sin a, which suggests one was derived from the other; that is the
subject of patch 0050.

Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with the translation unit
override-linked, gp_Cone(gp::XOY(), pi/6, 5) over u in [0, 2 pi], v in [0, 10].
Before: Mass() is 2040.524284763495 against the frustum 1587.0744437049404, and
the near-cylinder cases read 3.14473214923 at semiAngle 1e-3, 0.00314159580 at
1e-6 and 0.00000314159 at 1e-9, against the cylinder's 785.39816339744823.
After: Mass() is 1587.0744437049409, within 4.6e-13 of the frustum, and the
same three near-cylinder cases read 786.96961317468, 785.39973419443 and
785.39816496824, converging on the cylinder. The centre of mass is unchanged.

The inertia terms below dim carry a separate discrepancy of their own,
measured but deliberately not touched here: IR2 is built from a four term
quartic over 4 where the second moment about the axis integrates to a five term
quartic over 20, and it keeps the same spurious sin a. That is a distinct
defect with its own derivation, and fixing it here would change a second result
under cover of this one.

The reproducer is Scripts/repro/2992/probe.cxx and the transcript is
Scripts/repro/2992/override-link-transcript.txt in the OCCTSwift repository.
OCCTSwift issue #2992; the area half of the same issue is patch 0050.

diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_VelGProps.cxx
@@ -168,7 +168,9 @@ void GProp_VelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,
   double ZZ    = (Z2 - Z1) * (Z2 - Z1) * Cnt * Snt;
   double Auxi1 = 2 * R + (Z2 + Z1) * Snt;

-  dim = ZZ * (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Auxi1 / 2.;
+  // Frustum volume pi/3 H (R1^2 + R1 R2 + R2^2); the old form carried sin(a) and vanished at a = 0.
+  dim = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1)
+        * (3 * R * R + 3 * R * (Z2 + Z1) * Snt + (Z2 * Z2 + Z2 * Z1 + Z1 * Z1) * Snt * Snt) / 6.;

   double R1    = R + Z1 * Snt;
   double R2    = R + Z2 * Snt;
